_in_citation", "passed": true}, {"name": "values_roundtrip", "passed": true}, {"name": "heading_cue", "passed": true}], "reviewed_by": "claude_code", "review_note": "accepted A; Three conditions: h_s40 with the h_s41 minors exception kept inside the same item (guide, gold wave 1 rule), h_s42 unified qualification grades A-D, h_s43 suspension. A keeps the negation (…ないこと) with polarity requirement, which is the consistent form. B splits the minors sentence into its own item and marks the 第70条 item as disqualification while keeping the negation in text_ja, which is the inconsistent form. A's text_ja keeps the (1)/(2)/(3) numbering from the source, which is a copy of the sentence as written.", "final_state": "silver_model_reviewed", "prompt_version": "sv4", "labeler_overlap": true, "reviewed_choice": "web"}}
